  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Where tabaxi are charismatic, agile cat people, leonin are strong, bulky cat\n\tpeople. Tabaxi tend to resemble smaller cats like house cats or ocelots, while\n\tleonin resemble lions, including lions’ iconic manes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Mechanically, the Leonin is a Strength-based brute, having similar ability\n\tscore increases to the Half-Orc. Leonin get Darkvision, a free skill, and a\n\troar which can frighten nearby creatures, making them an excellent,\n\tinteresting, and accessible race."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "With the "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "custom origin rules",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/tcoe/character-options#CustomizingYourOrigin"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " in place, the Leonin and the Tabaxi are very similar. The Leonin gets one fewer skill proficiency, but gets Daunting Roar. Unfortunately, Daunting Roar is the Leonin’s only unique trait, so your class options are largely defined by whether or not Daunting Roar is a good choice for the class."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
